        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "improve(ui): replace the chat settings popover with a composer view menu",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe chat composer's gear popover had become a junk drawer: a Refresh action, a tri-state auto-scroll cycle button whose state was invisible, three display toggles, a \"History\" button that actually filtered cron sessions in the *sidebar* (and was wired to state nothing read — a dead control), a set-once send-shortcut preference, and a full voice/model/sensitivity/microphone block duplicating Settings → Talk. Most of it was misplaced, mislabeled (labels recycled from `cron.form.thinking`, `agents.tabs.tools`, `cron.actions.history`), or dead.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nControls should live next to what they control, and one-time preferences belong in Settings:\n\n- **Composer View menu** replaces the popover: a small eye-icon menu with three checkmark rows (Reasoning, Tool calls, Keep commentary) — the only genuinely chat-contextual toggles. Rows are disabled during onboarding, matching the old behavior.\n- **Refresh removed.** Chat is gateway-event-driven; the whole manual-refresh machinery (`handleChatManualRefresh`, generation/frame bookkeeping) is deleted.\n- **Auto-scroll modes removed.** \"Near-bottom\" (stick at bottom, release on scroll-up, jump-to-latest pill) is now the only behavior; the `chatAutoScroll` setting, its normalizer, and the mode branches in `scroll.ts` are gone.\n- **Cron-session filter moved to the sidebar** sessions sort/group menu as a working, persisted \"Show cron sessions\" checkbox (`resolveSessionNavigation` now takes `showCron`). The old popover toggle mutated `sessionsHideCron`, which no code consumed.\n- **Send shortcut moved to Settings → Appearance** in a new \"Chat\" block, alongside a **Microphone input** picker (the one client-side voice setting that persists, `realtimeTalkInputDeviceId`). Both are reachable via settings search.\n- **Ephemeral voice overrides deleted.** Voice/model/sensitivity are server talk config (`talk.realtime.*`, Settings → Talk); the in-memory per-tab overrides and the embedded talk-options renderer are removed. Talk sessions re-read persisted settings at start, so a microphone picked in Settings applies without a reload.\n\n## User Impact\n\n- The composer gains a compact View menu; the gear popover is gone.\n- Auto-scroll \"always\"/\"off\" modes disappear (default near-bottom behavior unchanged). The browser-local `chatAutoScroll` value is simply ignored — no migration needed for a client display pref.\n- Cron sessions can now actually be shown in the sidebar list (the previous toggle did nothing).\n- Send shortcut and microphone selection live in Settings → Appearance → Chat; voice/model/sensitivity are configured once in Settings → Talk instead of per-tab.\n\nNet −1,310 lines.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `pnpm check:changed` (lint + typecheck lanes) green on Blacksmith Testbox.\n- Unit/browser tests updated and run remotely: `chat-controls`, `scroll`, `chat-state`, `chat-send`, `chat-view`, `settings.node`, `navigation` (new cron-visibility test), `chat-responsive.browser`, config `view.browser`.\n- e2e specs updated for the new flows: view-menu toggle round-trip (`chat-composer-redesign`), send shortcut via Settings applying `aria-keyshortcuts` in chat (`chat-flow`), microphone picked in Settings driving `deviceId: { exact: \"usb\" }` at talk start and blocked-permission alert on the Settings page (`browser-talk-start-stop`).\n- Authenticated `ui:i18n:sync` run for the en.ts key changes (removed popover keys, added `chat.view.*`, `sessionsView.showCronSessions`, `configView.chatPrefs.*`).\n",
        "branch": "claude/settings-screen-redesign-034dcc",
